# Three.js Project Rules (Cursor)

- Follow existing project patterns; avoid unrelated refactors.
- Render loop must not allocate per frame (no new Vector3/Matrix4/etc. inside tick).
- Any created GPU resource must be disposed on teardown (geometry/material/texture/renderTargets).
- Do not add dependencies unless requested.
- Keep resize handling correct: camera aspect+updateProjectionMatrix, renderer size, composer size.
- Prefer instancing or batching for many repeated objects.
- Shadows are opt-in and must be justified; keep shadow settings conservative.
- Reference local docs:
  - `cursor/rules/commit-guidelines.mdc`
  - `cursor/rules/gitmoji-reference.mdc`
